(a) Except as specifically authorized in this article, tree protection areas shall remain in a natural, undisturbed condition; activities related to development within a tree protection area shall be prohibited. This specifically includes prohibition of the following within a tree protection area:
(1) Vehicle or equipment parking, storage or traffic;
(2) Materials or supplies storage;
(3) Placement of temporary or permanent structures;
(4) Equipment maintenance or washout;
(5) Wounding of tree trunks; wounding or breakage of limbs or branches greater than four inches in diameter; topping or other improper pruning, such as stub cuts or flush cuts;
(6) Fires or excessive heat from equipment exhausts;
(7) Site or lot clearing or grubbing;
(8) Soil excavation or soil cuts or fills;
(9) Grading; trenching; tilling; soil compaction;
(10) Top dressing with fill or soil greater than two inches in depth; and
(11) Paving.
(b) The zoning administrator may require that this section appear verbatim on tree protection and landscaping plans.
(Ord. of 4-9-2024, att.(909))
